SOAPBOX: Part-time effort, tuning the Big Knob as usual. Mostly S&P, but had a couple of short CQ-runs into Asia. Conditions were very good, if slightly down from last year. Always exciting to hear all the contest expeditions out there, doing their thing. I know how they feel.
SOAPBOX: I spent two days ahead of the contest re-installing my BOG wire system and coax feeders for the season. This simple 200-foot twinlead wire really enhances receive operation for me on 80 and 160m bands in two directions. Thanks to K1FZ for the hardware needed at each end.
